- Up to 120 requests per minute per account. If the limit is exceeded, wait at least 60 seconds before retrying.

When this tool fails:
- Error 400 (Bad request) means "Bad Request" and the suggested action is fix the request parameters and try again.
- Error 401 (Unauthorized) means "Unauthorized" and the suggested action is reconnect the OAuth integration before retrying.
- Error 403 (Forbidden) means "Account lacks permission or a plan-required feature." and the suggested action is do not retry; tell the user about the plan or permission limit.
- Error 404 (Not found) means "Resource not found in Marketing." and the suggested action is verify the identifier used in the call.
- Error 415 (Unsupported media type) means "Unsupported media type." and the suggested action is send a supported Content-Type (usually application/json) and try again.
- Error 422 (Unprocessable entity) means "Invalid payload for the Marketing API." and the suggested action is fix the fields listed in field_errors and try again.
- Error 429 (Too many requests) means "Conservative account rate limit of 120 requests per minute reached." and the suggested action is wait at least 60 seconds before retrying.
- Error 500 (Internal server error) means "Marketing is temporarily unavailable." and the suggested action is wait a few seconds and retry once.

What the AI should do:
- fix the request parameters and try again
- reconnect the OAuth integration before retrying
- do not retry; tell the user about the plan or permission limit
- verify the identifier used in the call
- send a supported Content-Type (usually application/json) and try again
- fix the fields listed in field_errors and try again
- wait at least 60 seconds before retrying
- wait a few seconds and retry once

